From 396481320ede5c94b8e95031e63d88339f929e3d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hui <vlado.kerando@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 22:03:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 06/43] Mod API: shared inventories on block entities and
 inventory menus (capability items)

A server mod gives its block entities up to 54 slots; any mod reads, inserts
(equal stacks first) and extracts within stack sizes, and the owner sets its
slots. Inventories are saved in data/horizon/items.json, and their items
drop where the block was after `removed` (or when set-slots takes slots
away). menus.open-inventory binds menu slots to an inventory as storage,
input or output: pickup and shift-click work as in a chest, and the menu
follows the inventory as it changes. The cells example turns redstone put
in its input slot into energy and makes redstone in its output slot.

