From c50f1e018d987a52203e5542901babf9d8562270 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hui <vlado.kerando@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 01:36:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 07/43] Mod API: machine recipe types for server mods
 (capability machine-recipes)

A server mod declares the recipe types of its machines: the game reads the
data/<id>/recipe/ JSON files of its id once, before the mods start, from its
own package and from a content mod's carry of the same id, parses each
file's type and the ingredient syntax of its inputs and results (tags
expanded through the item registry), and hands the mod the list with a
search by input - what a machine holding an item can make now, asked on its
tick, while all(kinds) is read once in init and kept. The whole file
reaches the mod as data, for the fields only it knows (energy, ticks,
tiers); nothing is saved with the world, being content. A mod with the
capability may carry only these files under its own id. The cells example
carries two grinding recipes that turn cobblestone and andesite in its
input slot into redstone, with a Load cobble button and /cellrecipes.

Horizon-Forge-Api: recipes-7
Co-Authored-By: ZCode AI agent (GLM-5.3)
