From: hui <vlado.kerando@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 06:08:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 17/43] Mod API: multiblock template files (multiblocks, part
 1: parsing)

The templates of capability `multiblocks`, read the way machine recipes
are: a server mod carries its structures as data/<id>/multiblock/*.json
files, one shape a file, named by layers of palette characters from the
bottom up (a block id, a list of them, "air" for a cell that must be
empty, "any" for one not checked; a space is always air) with the anchor
cell the mod's block entity sits on. The game reads the tree from the
mod's own package and from a content mod's carry of the same id before
the mod starts, skips a bad file with a line in the log (one file keeps
neither the mod nor the other structures from loading), and hands the
mod the list whole, with the file's own JSON as data. check_cells
matches a shape against the world through a closure, turned by quarter
turns, comparing block ids only, and answers the first mismatches.
Watches - the followed copies to come in part 3 - keep their store here
already: saved with the world, going with their anchor. Pure parsing
and logic: no WIT, no capability yet.

Co-Authored-By: ZCode AI agent (GLM-5.3)
