From 5e5c971deefcf7c0825c855690fcc048d729b5fa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hui <vlado.kerando@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 06:23:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 18/43] Mod API: multiblock templates and checks (capability
 multiblocks)

A server mod declares its multiblock structures (API level 14,
experimental, server mods only): the game reads the data/<id>/multiblock/
JSON files of its id once, before the mods start, from its own package and
from a content mod's carry of the same id, parses each file's layers,
palette and anchor into checked cells with their offsets from the anchor
(a block the manifest must ask for beside it: capability multiblocks needs
capabilities block-entities and world, and a mod with it may carry only
these files and its recipes under its own id), and hands the mod the list
whole with all() - read once in init and kept, like machine recipes.
check() matches one structure against the server's world with its anchor
at a position, turned by quarter turns clockwise from above, comparing
block ids only: none - it is whole; the first mismatches - at most 16,
each where in the world, the block the template takes there and what is
there, so fusion crafting can tell what is missing. A read of the world
it answers in the server's hooks; a running mod with the capability gets
the world lent for it. The cells example carries its energy core
(data/cells/multiblock/core.json, a ring of iron around the cell) and
/cellcore [pos] says it is whole or names the first block it needs.

Co-Authored-By: ZCode AI agent (GLM-5.3)
