From 324e914ab255596ce3cb92b82e9bee8da24e5619 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hui <vlado.kerando@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 06:36:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 19/43] Mod API: multiblock watch events (capability
 multiblocks)

A server mod asks the game to follow a copy of one of its structures
around one of its block entities: multiblocks.watch keeps it in the
world's save (data/horizon/multiblocks.json, beside the block entities
it anchors on, gone with them - a structure that was whole is told
broken with the entity's last data), and about once a second the game
matches every watch against the world again, within a budget of block
reads a pass, from where the last pass stopped. When a structure comes
together the mod hears multiblock_formed, when it no longer holds -
broken, rebuilt turned, blown up, mined by a guest - multiblock_broken,
each with the anchor's place, state, data and the quarter turn it is
whole at; a structure already whole at the watch call is reported by the
first check after it, and the answer of the call itself is of now, for
the world is lent in the server's hooks. A mod built before this keeps
working: the export is looked for, not needed. The SDK's ServerMod gains
the two hooks with empty defaults, and export_server_mod! wires them.

Co-Authored-By: ZCode AI agent (GLM-5.3)
