From 80b7ee34d8f48f0f77aed2c7e580148015a4d610 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hui <vlado.kerando@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 08:09:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 21/43] Mod API: the mods' saved data store (saved-data, part
 1: the store)

The store of capability `saved-data`, without its contract yet: bytes
each server mod keeps on the world itself, keyed by mod id and a key of
its own - not tied to a block, unlike block entities. The game owns the
store and saves it with the world in data/horizon/saved_data.json, so it
travels with the world folder, whichever game opens it next; a mod's own
`storage` folder, beside the mods, does not. A key holds at most 64 KiB,
a mod at most 256 keys and 1 MiB; a file that doesn't parse is kept aside
as .bad, as the block entities' is. The store rides in the block
entities' store - lent to the mods wherever it already is, saved with the
world wherever it already is - and a block_entities.json that doesn't
parse no longer takes it down: the mod data on the world itself is not
that file's to lose. Pure store: no WIT, no capability yet.

