From 8db3ac2960e2fdfd53592fe36724d2ccf04ea1d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hui <vlado.kerando@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 08:12:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 22/43] Mod API: world data on the mod, saved with the world
 (capability saved-data)

A server mod keeps bytes of its own on the world itself, not tied to a
block (API level 15, experimental, server mods only): the members of an
energy network, who owns a claim, a list of teleports. saved_data::get,
set, delete and keys read and change the store of part 1 - each mod its
own keys only, whatever key it guesses - through the block entities'
store, lent in the same server's hooks: a call outside them is an error,
not a crash, and a malformed key, over 64 KiB at one key, over 256 keys
or over 1 MiB for the whole mod is refused. The game writes the file once
per save of the world, so a mod's changes reach it with the next save,
and a disabled mod's data waits in it. The SDK re-exports the interface;
no new hooks, and a mod built before this keeps working, the import
landing in its component only when its code calls it. docs/mods.md tells
the two stores apart - the mod's `storage` folder beside the mods, this
one inside the world folder - and the reference is regenerated.

