From ffa42cb2ea79f754ab45bbbd74479a6a54bd9ccf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hui <vlado.kerando@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 08:21:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 23/43] Mod API: the cells example's power grids (capability
 saved-data)

The example's grids stand on the world itself, the very case the
capability is for: /cellnet <name> joins the cell under the player to a
power grid - the name is the saved-data key, so it takes a key's shape -
and /cellnet lists them with their cells. The members are lines in a
text value the mod reads back with a parse, keeping nothing in its own
memory: a restart of the mod (the scenario's reload step) loses nothing,
which is the point. A cell broken leaves its grids; the last cell takes
the grid with it, so the mod's data on the world does not outlive its
last cell. The cellnet command takes no pos argument on purpose: the
server's argument parser has no backtracking, so a pos before the name
would eat a grid name as a coordinate - the scenario walks the player to
the second cell instead. Unit tests cover the member lines' round trip,
the last member taking the grid with it, and the grid names.

Horizon-Forge-Api: saved-data-9
Co-Authored-By: ZCode AI agent (GLM-5.3)
