From b220214fd4178029eb832b52845bc4f9dcced0e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hui <vlado.kerando@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 10:35:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 25/43] Mod API: item hooks in the game (capability item-hooks)

The game calls the item hooks where the clicks and blows happen. A use
of a claimed item in the main hand - after the block interactions and
the cooldown, before the vanilla use of the item - is the mod's alone:
the mod hears it at the tick's end with the stack as it was clicked,
and the block under the crosshair if there was one (a block a mod takes
the use of still wins, a sneaking player keeps vanilla's, the off hand
stays vanilla's). A blow with a claimed item - on a mob, or on a player
in PvP, host or guest - asks the claiming mods before the damage lands,
their answers chained; a player hurt through the game's direct-hurt
funnel (falling, a firework, magic effects, the pearl, the dragon,
lightning, thorns) has its claimed armour take a share first, the four
hurts that went around the funnel routed into it. The players'
inventories are lent to the hooks as copies - 41 slots a player, hotbar
first, armour feet to head, the off hand - taken back with each
set-data write in place, so a guest's client is told on its next flush;
the guest whose turn it is keeps their stacks in the game, the host's
in their record, and the lend covers both. The block entities' store
and the inventories are lent whatever capabilities the running mods
have - item hooks run in the same server's hooks as the world does -
and a connection's command lends the hub too, so /staff reads the
typist's stacks.

Horizon-Forge-Api: item-hooks-9
Co-Authored-By: ZCode AI agent (GLM-5.3)
