From 75868f9f60dc73876a9c588428e8079ad008ae4f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hui <vlado.kerando@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 11:04:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 26/43] Mod API: the cells example's energy staff (capability
 item-hooks)

The example claims a blaze rod as an energy staff and a golden helmet
as a small shield of its own - the capability's whole shape in one item.
The staff's charge is the mod's bytes on the stack itself: /staff reads
it, a use in the air spends 100 FE of it, a blow with the staff deals
twice over while it has the 10 FE that costs, and a use on one of the
mod's cells - or a tick standing on one - moves 1000 FE between the
stack and the cell, the emptier side filling. The helmet worn takes 5
points of a hurt for as many FE as it holds, an FE a point, and says
when it is out. A stack of rods is refused its charge with the reason:
a split copies a stack's components to both halves, so charge is kept
one item at a time. The scenario drives it all - the charge survives a
reload of the mod, for it lives on the stack - and the script runner
gains the step keys for it: hold gives a player a stack (the main hand
slot 0, armour 36..39 feet to head), use-item uses it (on a block too),
attack strikes an entity with it, hurt hurts the player. TestGame keeps
the players' stacks and lends them as the game does, its set-data
writes carried back onto them.

