 halves, and screens (capability network)

A server mod and a client mod that share an id talk over one custom
payload channel (horizon:mod_net) in the play state: send-to and
client-sent on the server, send and server-sent on the client, bytes on
mod-named channels (30,000 bytes, 64 messages and 256 KiB a call, 32
messages a tick from a player). The server announces the channel in
configuration like the quiet commands; only Horizon clients are sent to.
With the client half's ui widgets this is a real screen: the cells example
opens one with /cellui, showing a cell's charge, a bar, its redstone and
Fill and Drain buttons, and the server keeps the cell each screen shows so
a client can't name another. Test scripts gain net, select and ui-close
steps and expect.net and expect.screen. Mod text widget colours are now
read as the documented 0xRRGGBB (they were drawn with red and blue swapped).

