From 22d8a4cc21ed75ef40e9e5892b097309fa494133 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hui <vlado.kerando@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 13:00:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 30/43] Mod API: mobs of a mod's own (capability entities)

A server mod spawns vanilla mobs it marks and then steers: spawn with a
kind, a tag and flags (no AI, invisible, silent, invulnerable, no gravity,
takes use, name, health), get/list its mobs, teleport, push, set health,
remove. It hears each tick, a player's blow before it lands (answering with
the damage to deal, 0 to 4x), the death, the removal and a right click on a
mob that takes the use. The game finds a mod's mobs again after a restart by
marks in their saved Tags (horizon_mod:<id>, horizon_tag:<tag>,
horizon_use). A spawn is refused in hooks the game runs mid-tick.

The cells example gains /sentinel: an iron golem that takes a third of a
blow, mends a point a second, answers a right click with its health and
says when it falls. Test scripts gain strike, interact, expect.entities and
expect.dealt.

While a guest's packet is handled (single player included) the hub is out
of the game, so the acting player is now built from the game's own state;
item hooks' blows had no acting player there and never reached the mod.

Horizon-Forge-Api: entities-11

