From 6edb0e20a34cfc3a971e6a372ecf020f68ce020a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hui <vlado.kerando@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 13:13:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 31/43] Mod API: fluid tanks on block entities (capability
 fluids)

A mod gives its own block entities 1 to 8 tanks (capacity up to 2^50 mB,
most in and out per call); every mod fills and drains any tank, and push
moves fluid into the tanks on a block's six sides like a pipe. A tank
holds one fluid at a time, named namespace:path (vanilla or the mod's
own), and never mixes; insert fills a tank holding the fluid before an
empty one. fluid-of-bucket and bucket-of-fluid map the vanilla buckets.
Tanks live beside the energy buffers in the block entity store: lent with
it, saved in data/horizon/fluids.json, dropped with their block entity.

The cells example gives each lodestone a 16-bucket tank that keeps half a
bucket and passes the rest to the cells beside it; /cellfluid reads,
fills and drains it. Verified in the game, including a restart.

