From 5e0e82c440a246ea701199357eded9f57a7a602c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hui <vlado.kerando@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 13:35:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 32/43] Mod API: redstone for a mod's blocks (capability
 redstone)

The game reads the signal on each face of every block entity a redstone
mod owns, once a tick, and tells the mod (redstone_changed) when it
changes, when it is read for the first time, or when a neighbour changed;
get-input reads it any time. A mod sets the signal each face gives out
(set-output: weak like a redstone block, or strong like a lever); vanilla
blocks around it read it through the engine's own getSignal and
getDirectSignal, so wire, lamps, repeaters, doors and pistons react, and
the blocks around update as they do for a lever. Outputs are saved in
data/horizon/redstone.json and go with their block entity.

horizon-world gains LevelAccess::mod_signal (default 0) consulted by the
signal queries, and Behaviours::neighbor_signals. The game keeps the
current dimension's emitters in a map the level view reads.

The cells example gives out a gauge of its charge (a level for each 1000
FE) and stops charging while a signal reaches its top face. Test scripts
gain signals and expect.redstone. Verified in the game: a lamp beside a
cell lights, and a redstone block on top halves the charge rate.

Horizon-Forge-Api: redstone-13

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
