From 407a6dbefecdb6573ed356947d2fb277544aaac2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hui <vlado.kerando@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 13:49:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 33/43] Mod API: particles and sounds (capability effects)

A server mod sends particles and plays sounds in the world: spawn-particle
(any particle the game has by name, a point, spread, speed, count; colour
and scale for dust and the spell particles, a block state for the block
ones; flash, items, trails and vibrations are not sent) to the players
within 32 blocks (always-show: 512), and play-sound / play-sound-to with a
volume, a pitch and a category (the volume slider it plays on). They are
the game's own packets, built from the hub the window is a guest of, so
single player, LAN and vanilla clients all get them. At most 128 effects a
hook call.

The cells example gains /cellfx (a puff of dust and a chime that rises
with the gauge) and a sentinel's fall smokes and sounds. Test scripts gain
expect.effects. Verified in the game: the dust and large smoke particles
reach the window and the chime and golem sounds are heard.

Horizon-Forge-Api: effects-14

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
