From 4beda97d049c283090a7e9a2fdbd5e4f72624f2e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hui <vlado.kerando@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 14:00:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 34/43] Mod API: game events (capability game-events)

The server tells a mod what happens to players and the world, as a mod bus
does: player_damaged (health fell, any source), player_died (with the
death message as vanilla writes it), player_respawned, dimension_changed,
game_mode_changed, mob_killed (a player's melee blow) and weather_changed.
They are notices after the fact; a mod that must change an outcome uses
the hook of the capability that owns it. Health, dimension and game mode
are compared once a tick for every player, so the window's own player, LAN
guests and a dedicated server's players are all covered; the death
message and the kill come from the game's own death and attack paths.

The capability adds no function a mod calls, so the API level stays 21.
The cells example answers a death, a dimension change, a kill and the
weather. Test scripts gain game-events. Verified in the game: weather,
a zombie felled, the Nether entered and a death with its message.

