From e15bbadc0f52d24a49552b40b98f58f5ff0225d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hui <vlado.kerando@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 14:15:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 35/43] Mod API: settings in a file the player edits
 (capability config)

A server mod declares its settings once (config::declare: a key, a
description, a kind and a default; a flag, a whole number or a number inside
limits, text, or one of some choices) and reads them with get. The game
keeps them in config/<mod id>.toml beside the mod, written with each
entry's description and limits as comments, looks at it every five
seconds, and tells the mod which entries a hand edit changed
(config_changed). A value that is missing, of the wrong kind or outside its
limits is the default again (the file is written back and the log says
why); a file that does not parse is left alone and said once. config::set
checks and writes for a command or screen of the mod's own.

The cells example reads its charge, core multiplier, sentinel damage
divisor and name, /cellfx's sound and whether it announces deaths from the
file, and has /cellconfig [key] [value]. Test scripts gain config-file and
expect.config-file. Verified in the game: the file is written, a hand edit
reaches the mod within seconds, /cellconfig sets and refuses, and a broken
file is reported.

