From e326141f68504c795a8417f2186a07b8a3738978 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hui <vlado.kerando@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 17:23:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 36/43] Mod API: item displays, moved and riding (capability
 item-displays), part 1: contract, runtime and the server's game

Capability `displays` gains three functions (API level 23). show-item
shows a display as an item's model: an item id, a count of 1 to 99 and
components in vanilla's item syntax (up to 512 bytes) - a look, not
storage - through the same transform and interpolation as its shapes, as
a vanilla `item_display` entity. move walks a display of any shape to a
position without remaking it: the server sends the entity's
teleport_duration and an EntityPositionSync, so every client that already
knows displays walks it there (at most 59 ticks); a display riding a mob
is put down first. ride makes a display ride one of the mod's own mobs
(capability `entities`), carried along - it sits where the mob stands,
lifted by its own transform - or puts it down; at most 16 displays ride
one mob, and a repeat ride sends nothing.

The hub's riding book, rebuilt every tick, now carries the mods'
display passengers too (a dead carrier drops its rider there), so
SetPassengers reaches every client that tracks the mob, again when the
mob re-enters its tracking range, and the display joins the mob's own
riders in one list; a guest that just received the display gets the
carrier's passengers with it. `cargo horizon-mod check` names the three
new outputs (and the ones earlier stages had left it not compiling).

Verified by the stage's scenario and unit tests (part 3); a vanilla LAN
guest sees the packets from this part alone.

Horizon-Forge-Api: item-displays-17

Co-Authored-By: ZCode AI agent (GLM-5.3)
