From ce26104370341dd56cabc5880935689e15f06404 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hui <vlado.kerando@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 17:23:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 37/43] Mod API: item displays, moved and riding (capability
 item-displays), part 2: the game's own client draws item displays and carries
 riders

Horizon's own window now draws what the server's packets of part 1
carry. An `item_display` joins the text and block displays
(`handleAddEntity`), its stack arrives as entity data (the network stack
decoded with the registries, as an item frame's is) and is drawn
resolved with no display context, as vanilla's ItemDisplayRenderer does,
through the display's own transform at the world's light. SetPassengers
marks displays as it marks mobs and players: while a display rides, the
carrier's interpolated position is the display's - the mod lifts it by
its transform - and its own move waits until it is put down. Item
displays draw nothing until their stack arrives, as block displays show
air. The smooth move of part 1 already worked here: the client walks a
display over its teleport_duration, which the server now sends.

Verified by unit tests on the display's data, drawing and riding.

Horizon-Forge-Api: item-displays-17

Co-Authored-By: ZCode AI agent (GLM-5.3)
