From 7f221226e267d089c56746655f73b151f35bb433 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hui <vlado.kerando@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 17:23:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 38/43] Mod API: item displays, moved and riding (capability
 item-displays), part 3: the cells example, tests and docs

The SDK re-exports the display stack (DisplayStack::new(item).count(n)
.components(c)), and the cells example shows both shapes of the new
functions: four nether stars circle each cell's spinning core - shown
once with show-item when the cell first appears, then only moved every
refresh, so the client walks them round without a flicker - and a
sentinel carries a star above its head, riding the golem wherever it
walks, re-shown and re-ridden in entity_tick after a restart (displays
are never saved; the mobs' ids are new then). The star goes with the
golem's death or removal, the orbit with the cell.

Test scripts gain expect.displays (kind, what, place, and the riding
mob), settled in the sandbox harness as the game settles its display
entities; the example's new script walks a cell's orbit round two
refreshes, rides a star on a sentinel and takes both away. The docs
tell the three functions and their limits, and the honest line about
free model files replaces the one about item displays.

Verified by the examples' scripts (16 now), the crate's unit tests and
the cells unit tests; not yet verified by hand in the game's window.

Horizon-Forge-Api: item-displays-17

Co-Authored-By: ZCode AI agent (GLM-5.3)
