From e93469bf7f64d69c75a720f45042fb4401fe0124 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hui <vlado.kerando@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 18:32:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 39/43] The dev checks pass on Windows: the hook's Python,
 pr_ready's floor, the relay test's cut

The pre-push hook execs python3; Windows installs often have only the
Store's stub under that name (it prints "Python" and exits 49) while the
real interpreter answers as python, so the hook now uses python3 only
when one answers and falls back to python. The checker it runs is
unchanged, and its tests pass on Windows now.

pr_ready refuses to run under Python 3.10: the Python tests it drives
need 3.11 (tomllib, hashlib.file_digest), and running them older showed
26 failures that are the interpreter's, not the code's. On Windows:
py -3.12 tools/pr_ready.py.

The relay's first-line cut reaches a Windows client only as an end of
stream - a write into the closed connection keeps succeeding there - so
the test watched for a failure that never comes (it failed identically
on origin/main). It now ends when either arrives: the write failure Unix
reports, or the end of the stream Windows does, with the same
three-second bound. The relay itself was verified to cut the trickling
line at its one-second deadline; only the test's ear was on the wrong
side.

Co-Authored-By: ZCode AI agent (GLM-5.3)
---
 .githooks/pre-push                   |  8 +++++++-
 crates/horizon-relay/tests/tunnel.rs | 19 ++++++++++++++++++-
 tools/pr_ready.py                    |  7 +++++++
 3 files changed, 32 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.githooks/pre-push b/.githooks/pre-push
index d067dd226..e2f1214a6 100755
--- a/.githooks/pre-push
+++ b/.githooks/pre-push
@@ -1,2 +1,8 @@
 #!/bin/sh
-exec python3 tools/check_public_tree.py --pre-push
+# python3 where there is one; some Windows installs have only the Store's
+# stub under that name (it prints "Python" and exits 49) and a real
+# interpreter as `python`.
+if python3 -c "pass" >/dev/null 2>&1; then
+    exec python3 tools/check_public_tree.py --pre-push
+fi
+exec python tools/check_public_tree.py --pre-push
