From e1d52b1c38b598add5fb4a1b2d4ae30f30929c38 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hui <vlado.kerando@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 19:30:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 40/43] Mod API: a server mod may carry content (capability
 server-content), part 1: the contract and the loader

A server mod may now have capability registries with api = "0.3" and
side = "server": its .hmod carries assets/ and data/ beside mod.wasm,
the same files under the same fence as a 0.2 content mod's - blocks and
items declared in data/<id>/horizon/, files in the mod's own namespaces
(its id and those its manifest lists, so `namespaces` follows the common
rules for it too), additions to vanilla and convention tags, with the
same caps. One package is a mod again: no second content mod of the same
id to carry the files.

The gate is both_sides(), not on_server(): a content capability belongs
to either side, and 0.2 content mods of side "client"/"both" parse as
before. API 0.1 still refuses registries, now naming both lines that may
carry it. The loader needed no change - content_root and Content::read
were already side-agnostic - so a server mod's content builds the same
overlay (its states after vanilla's, in id order) in every window that
has the mod on, and a mod whose content is refused stays off with the
