From 0f7551c62cb8b917fa9af52a8f08adf7b45df7de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hui <vlado.kerando@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 21:57:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 42/43] Mod API: messages between server mods (capability
 inter-mod), part 1: the contract, the SDK and the manifest

A server mod may serve other server mods, as a library mod's code shared
by whoever needs it (API level 24). The WIT contract gains interface
`inter-mod` - expose, providers, subscribe, publish and send-to - and the
`inter-mod-events` export the game calls with a message; both are wired
into `horizon-block-mod`, so the SDK builds every server mod against
them, and a world of the mod's own (`inter-mod-host`) keeps mods built
before it loading unchanged, hearing nothing. A message is bytes on a
channel of the sending mod's own naming, as `network`'s, delivered at the
end of the server's tick in rounds, so a library's answer reaches its
asker within the same tick (the bus and the delivery are part 2).

The manifest may now list `provides = ["spin-lib@1.0"]` and `requires =
["spin-lib@1"]` (capability `inter-mod`, experimental, server mods only):
the entries' shape is checked on parse, and a need is served by the same
name and major version at least as new. The SDK gains the
`ServerMod::message` hook with a default that hears nothing, wired into
`export_server_mod!` beside the other events. docs/api/mods-reference.md
is regenerated from the contract.

Verified by cargo test -p horizon-mods --lib (72 passed), the api_reference
test (4 passed, with the file rewritten by HORIZON_WRITE_DOCS=1) and the
sandbox battery (32 passed: every example still builds against the world
with its new export). Not yet verified by hand in the game's window.

Horizon-Forge-Api: inter-mod-19

Co-Authored-By: ZCode AI agent (GLM-5.3)
